{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":22,"code":"SNG","name":"Song of Songs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":1,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"SNG 1:1"},"The song of songs, which ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," Solomon’s. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"SNG 1:2"},"Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth: for thy love ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is "]},"better than wine. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"SNG 1:3"},"Because of the savour of thy good ointments thy name ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is as "]},"ointment poured forth, therefore do the virgins love thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"SNG 1:4"},"Draw me, we will run after thee: the king hath brought me into his chambers: we will be glad and rejoice in thee, we will remember thy love more than wine: the upright love thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"SNG 1:5"},"I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," black, but comely, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, as the tents of Kedar, as the curtains of Solomon. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"SNG 1:6"},"Look not upon me, because I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," black, because the sun hath looked upon me: my mother’s children were angry with me; they made me the keeper of the vineyards; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["but"]}," mine own vineyard have I not kept. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"SNG 1:7"},"Tell me, O thou whom my soul loveth, where thou feedest, where thou makest ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thy flock"]}," to rest at noon: for why should I be as one that turneth aside by the flocks of thy companions? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"SNG 1:8"},"If thou know not, O thou fairest among women, go thy way forth by the footsteps of the flock, and feed thy kids beside the shepherds’ tents. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"SNG 1:9"},"I have compared thee, O my love, to a company of horses in Pharaoh’s chariots. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"SNG 1:10"},"Thy cheeks are comely with rows ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of jewels,"]}," thy neck with chains ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of gold. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"SNG 1:11"},"We will make thee borders of gold with studs of silver. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:11"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"SNG 1:12"},"While the king ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["sitteth"]}," at his table, my spikenard sendeth forth the smell thereof. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"SNG 1:13"},"A bundle of myrrh ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," my wellbeloved unto me; he shall lie all night betwixt my breasts. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"SNG 1:14"},"My beloved ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," unto me ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as"]}," a cluster of camphire in the vineyards of En-gedi. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"SNG 1:15"},"Behold, thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art"]}," fair, my love; behold, thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art "]},"fair; thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["hast"]}," doves’ eyes. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"SNG 1:16"},"Behold, thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art"]}," fair, my beloved, yea, pleasant: also our bed ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," green. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"SNG 1:17"},"The beams of our house ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," cedar, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," our rafters of fir. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 1:17"}]}]}
